  "description": {
    "sub_id3": null,
    "sub_name": "非晶質材料",
    "sub_ename": "AMORPHOUS MATERIALS",
    "describe_ch": "非晶質材料涵蓋金屬、高分子與陶瓷材料在非結晶態之物質，所表現出與結晶態物質特性迥異。回顧科技產業所涉及非晶質材料的使用現況與發展趨勢，介紹各類玻璃材料、金屬玻璃、高分子材料的巨觀與微觀結構。讓學生掌握非晶質材料在電子、電化學、光學及磁性的特性及應用，以建築玻璃、顯示器面板、光纖維、變壓器磁芯、太陽能電池板、電腦記憶體、軟性電子料元件為案例。",
    "describe_eh": "The amorphous materials take a major part of the material family with unique properties different from their crystalline counterparts. Beginning with a quick review of status and new development of amorphous materials, students will acquire a wide range of concepts on macroscopic and microscopic structures and modeling of glasses, metallic glasses, and polymers. Applications examples of building glass panels, display panels, optic fibers, magnetic cores of transformers, solar cells, computer memories, wearable electronic components in aspects of electronics, electrochemistry, and magnetic aspects for amorphous materials.",
    "pre_subname": "",
    "pre_sub_id3": null,
    "pre_sub_ename": "",
    "pre_describe": null,
    "pre_describe_en": null,
    "scr_credit": 3.0
  },
  "targets": [
    {
      "seq": 1,
      "describe_ch": "應用對非晶質材料之目前研究計畫案之知識及興趣。材料科學與工程的專業領域。\t",
      "describe_en": "To apply necessary knowledge and interests on amorphous materials to serve the purpose of the ongoing research and development projects."
    },
    {
      "seq": 2,
      "describe_ch": "了解非晶質材料之發展沿革及最新動態，並能建立非晶質材料設計能力及其之應用向面。材料科學與工程的專業領域。\t",
      "describe_en": "To understand the developments and frontiers on amorphous materials and key concepts and material design capability of the applications and products of amorphous materials."
    },
    {
      "seq": 3,
      "describe_ch": "分析非晶質材料領域之相關技術文獻及資料具有基本之解讀及研判能力。策劃及執行材料專題研究的能力。\t",
      "describe_en": "To analyze all the accessed databases on special topics on amorphous materials to display their professional judgments."
    },
    {
      "seq": 4,
      "describe_ch": "綜合書面或口頭報告技巧對所獲之非晶質材料論文及研發結果與同僚、助教及教師清楚陳述溝通。建立良好的國際觀。\t",
      "describe_en": "To synthesize students’ verbal and written skill as discussing or explaining the technical context and R&D results of amorphous materials to the peers and the adviser."
    }
  ],
